-2.2172682292875834e-05,-3.611976353568025e-05,-0.0006596058374270797,0.0,-9.42901024245657e-05,0.0,0.0,-0.08308587223291397,-0.01191687397658825,-4.768370445162873e-07,-0.012046913616359234,-4.815939246327616e-05,-5.722029527532868e-06,-4.291525328881107e-06,-2.3841855067985307e-07,0.0,-8.344646857949556e-07,-0.00019798702851403505,-1.0728830375228426e-06,0.0,-3.3378546504536644e-06,-2.861018856492592e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,46254,510,59,9640,59,15940,1124,37018,35702,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,18,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,20,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,22,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,24,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,16,16,59,2493,15170,16,17,27275,59,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nCompute:\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12}.\n\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8bc3dd5d0b7fe41a1256a3e1e2b4a4097eafaa07177862198427d53a22408845"},"seconds":58.64306330680847,"seed":1124419325804732786,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the given problem, we will use trigonometric identities and properties to find the value of the sum:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the angles in the sine functions:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12}, \\quad \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4}, \\quad \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}, \\quad \\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12}, \\quad \\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{4}, \\quad \\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity \\(\\sin (\\pi - x) = \\sin x\\) to simplify the terms:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\left(\\pi - \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right) = \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\left(\\pi - \\frac{3\\pi}{12}\\right) = \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\left(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right) = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the original sum can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n2 \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + 2 \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2 \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out the 2:\n\n\\[\n2 \\left( \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right).\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the values of \\(\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\), \\(\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\), and \\(\\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\). We know:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nFor \\(\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\) and \\(\\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\), we use the angle addition formulas. However, we can use symmetry and known sums of sines in a regular polygon to find that:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4} + \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the original sum is:\n\n\\[\n2 \\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right) = \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}.\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
